# Zepto Prototype Rules

Use the existing Google Stitch-generated screens as the UI foundation.

Do NOT recreate or redesign the UI.

## Primary Objective

Wire existing screens together and make them functional while preserving the original design.

## Technical Rules

- Use React + TypeScript
- Use Tailwind CSS
- Use React Router
- Keep all demo data inside local JSON files
- No backend, database, authentication, external APIs, or paid libraries
- Preserve existing components whenever possible

## UI Rules

- Never redesign Zepto
- Never generate replacement screens
- Keep layouts, spacing, colors and components from Google Stitch
- Only add interactions and navigation

## Recommendation Rules

- Recommendations come from shoppingMissions.json
- Never generate random recommendations
- Do not recommend products already present in the active shopping list

## Prototype Flows

1. My Space → Breakfast List → Recommendations → Product Page
2. Buddies → Arindam Chat → Shared Product → Product Page
3. Shared List → Weekend Party → Recommendations → Product Page
